<!--Post: 36--><!--Time: 1085201023-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST36"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cosmoj<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cosmoj<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 21, 2004 - 9:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I posted something similar on the C &amp; J board way back when the March letter first came out, but there are so many more posters now, that maybe someone would to discuss. <BR> <BR>When the letter first came out, Susan Peters &#40;Channel 3 I think&#41; interviewed Drowatsky who is now retired and was the lead detective during the Otero years.   He made an interesting comment that puzzles me and though I can&#39;t recall it verbatim he and Susan were talking about how the investigation was led away from solving the crime as police officers started accusing police officers, etc.  He then said something to the effect that the accusations started because there was a bloody bootprint at the Otero&#39;s which was made by the type of boot that the WPD wore at the time. However, they had concluded that bootprint was there before the officers showed up.  The fact that BTK wore police style boots doesn&#39;t suprise me and really I don&#39;t feel he is a police officer.  What puzzles me is where the blood came from.  I thought they were all strangled and it was reported they each had bruising around the face and cheeks.  I never heard about any of the Otero&#39;s being stabbed or anything else that would cause bleeding.  I would imagine as gruesome as it seems that strangling might cause someone to vomit some blood, I don&#39;t know, but even so, would it be enough blood for there to be a full bootprint?  Any thoughts?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 36-->
<!--Post: 91--><!--Time: 1085540528-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST91"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Clarice<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Clarice<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, May 25, 2004 - 8:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Cosmoj; I was troubled by the same matter.The kansas.com board has discussed this issue.  The rumor is that there was blood at the Otero house.  It is not resolved if a careless cop stepped in the blood or if BTK had cop boots on.  However, consider the following and draw your own conclusions &#40;read between the lines&#41; based on the assumption that there is probably a lot that LE is not releasing.  BTK had a knife with him as confirmed by the Vian survivors and the Bright survivor.  To me this indicates that he may have carried a knife to the other crimes as well.  Did he use it on the victims?  We know that he did use it on Bright and I think Weigerle &#40;not sure on Weigerle&#41;.   <BR>Binding and strangling would not cause enough blood for a foot print. <BR>On the John Douglas site, he indicates that BTK sent a sketch to the home of the &#34;older woman&#34; that he did not kill &#40;he got tired waiting for her and left- remember this one?&#41;.  The sketch showed the insertion of a Billy Club or &#34;sap&#34; into the victim. <BR>It has been stated that he &#34;spent a lot of time&#34; with Julie Otero.  What if he used a billy club on her and/or Mrs. Otero?  This would cause a female to bleed.   <BR>Sorry for the explicit post, but as I said I had the same question re blood that you had.  This is how I have put it all together. <BR>One more item, John Douglas profiled BTK as a &#34;wanna be cop&#34; for several reasons.  One reason could be the footware?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 91-->
<!--Post: 99--><!--Time: 1085598727-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST99"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Prairie_chicken<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Prairie_chicken<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 26, 2004 - 12:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Cosmoj, this is a copy and paste from my post at C&amp;J.  I think it follows some of your ideas:This is bothering me: <BR>        I was looking at the sketches of the Otero house and position of the bodies. The parents and son were found first upstairs. The stairway to the basement started in the hallway and descended down toward the east wall of the basement. The sketches show Josie was hung from pipes close to the west wall of the basement. Now, &#40;I’ve spent all morning trying to find this&#41; from:  <BR> <BR> <BR>The Wichita Eagle--one of the 2004 articles. <BR> <BR>&#34;It was one of the most blood-curdling scenes I ever worked, and I worked a lot of murders in Wichita,&#34; said former Wichita police detective Gary Caldwell, who was among the first on the scene… <BR> <BR>Caldwell didn&#39;t see her when he descended to the basement without a flashlight. Groping around for a light switch, he bumped into the body -- an experience that later gave him nightmares… <BR> <BR>Hoping the killer would return that night: <BR>&#34;It was like Grand Central Station,&#34; said police detective Bernie Drowatzky. He and Caldwell sat in the Otero house all night with a psychic, watching traffic and hoping the killer would return. <BR> <BR>Here&#39;s my put: <BR> <BR>Now, Gary Caldwell was a member of the WPD, one of the first on the scene &#40;was he expecting the call knowing they would be found that afternoon, did he need to be one of the first to explain any possible bloody footprints or fingerprints, did he want to watch it all unfold?&#41; <BR> <BR>Caldwell bumps into Josie’s body in the dark? How could he when at 4:30 or 5:00 in the evening, even in January, there would be some light through the basement windows or from upstairs. It wouldn’t be totally pitch black dark. Besides that, he gets to the bottom of the stairs on the east side of the basement and is still groping for a light switch clear on the other side of the basement? Or maybe he knew she needed to be found over there.  <BR> <BR>Then, he sits in the house all night with a psychic and another detective hoping the killer returns to the scene. The way he loves to play games, that would be the ultimate.  <BR> <BR>Gary Caldwell no longer works for the WPD and I wonder if he is the same Gary Caldwell that is now the Sheriff of Clay Co? <BR> <BR>Would you please check out your 1974 phone directory and see where this guy lived in 1974? <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 99-->
<!--Post: 186--><!--Time: 1086337680-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST186"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->J_eric<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->J_eric<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 04, 2004 - 1:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Are you telling us that the police, in investigating a brand-new multiple murder, radioed for a psychic but not a police dog? <BR> <BR>Cops without flashlights?  All Los Angeles officers carry big mag-lights, the better to bop evildoers over the head with.  <BR> <BR>This sounds more like a Moe, Larry and Shemp farce! <BR> <BR> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 186-->
<!--Post: 239--><!--Time: 1086839806-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST239"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cosmoj<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cosmoj<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, June 09, 2004 - 8:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Clarice,   I have a 1974 city directory which only lists names by addresses and a 1976 phone book.  In the 1976 Phone book there isn&#39;t a listing for a Gary Caldwell, but there is a listing for a GL Caldwell at 1920 e 10th.  I have a 1980 &amp; 1986 city directory and neither lists this person at that address. <BR> <BR>I have often wondered about the light switch also.  There were 5 kids in the family and 3 bedrooms on the main floor.  It&#39;s possible that all 5 shared 2 bedrooms, but I think it&#39;s unlikely.  Which means someone had to have a bedroom in the basement.  Therefore I find it hard to believe there wasn&#39;t a light switch right at the bottom of the stairs.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 239-->
<!--Post: 258--><!--Time: 1086969270-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST258"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jenkins<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jenkins<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 11, 2004 - 8:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->well the position of the light switch is impossible to determine at this time without entering that basement. <BR> <BR>Knowing the area, I would guess that the basement was unfinished and knowing how unfinished basements are around here its not out of the question for me to guess that the light was just a bulb protruding from the ceiling and that it had a string or cord of sorts to be used for turning it on or off, in which case you would have to walk around a bit to find. I mean you would expect there to be a light switch at the top or bottom of the stairs, but that is a bit of a shabby area and its not out of the question that the basement was an unfinished one with merely a cord for turning on the light. As far as the theory on how dark it was in the basement, there is really no way to tell. The living room in my parents basement is pitch black dark as there is not a single window. There are 3 windows in that basement but they are in other rooms. Now I do believe that the basement of the Otero house was probably just one big room and that the windows should have provided a bit of light at 4:30 or 5. Not much but enough to see a body. However, in a shoddy neighborhood, you generally have shoddy insulation. It is not uncommon for people to put things in their basement windows to prevent air from leaking in or out. In the basement of my parents house, each of those windows is entirely blocked by thick styrofoam, thus making the basement pitch black anytime of day anytime of the year. It is not unlikely that the Oteros did the same. <BR> <BR>Oh and J, yes it is very much a 3 stooges operation here, but god bless&#39;em they sure do try and hell they even worked without a contract for a bit here recently, good boys in blue good boys, just not the best and the brightest. <BR> <BR> <BR>Still lacking coherency sorry guys. Maybe after lunch I&#39;ll make more sense.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 258-->
<!--Post: 982--><!--Time: 1094218277-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST982"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, September 03, 2004 - 6:31 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Clarice: I read last night on another message board that he did bad things to Julie Otero over and above what we know. The person stating that said that someone involved in the investigation told her &#39;more than she wanted to know&#39;. I will try to locate the site again. Evidently, in one of BTK&#39;s letters he talked about Julie and how she excited him with her &#39;pleading eyes&#39; as he tightened the rope around her neck. <BR> <BR>Should the police now release publicly what has been known about the case, the outcry would be horrendous. Again and again, the tax payers are duped by public officials and those who are sworn to protect and serve. There is prudence in avoiding a panic, but forewarned is forearmed.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 982-->
<!--Post: 1645--><!--Time: 1102514572-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1645"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ace<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ace<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 08, 2004 - 6:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very Interesting observations. In my opinion Julie was the target and she was hung so I would suppose the blood came from her &#40;gravity&#41;. She was probably sexually assaulted with an object since the killer was sexually dis-fuctional. Did not have intercourse with his victims. The blood probably came from Julire and since police were not trained properly in the early seventies in protecting crime scenes and working crime scenes I would think the bloody boot print came from a cop. One thing for sure now there is NO way to tell. That&#39;s why protecting crime scenes are so important and today this day cops are still not doing it when they know better. Everyone wants to see the dead body including the police. I was recently involved in a triple homicide case and the same thing happened found a boot print and couldn&#39;t determine who left it the police or the killer. I don&#39;t think for one minute the BTK is a cop. So the WPD can stop waisting there time on that notion! <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1645-->
<!--Post: 1646--><!--Time: 1102516865-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1646"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 08, 2004 - 6:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My mistake when I wrote Julie. It should have been Josephine, the little girl. I don&#39;t think that she was the target. I think that the children were eliminated because they could id the killer. The famuily may well have known him or been familiar with him. Killing the father may or may not have been in the plan. What better way to settle a debt than have a man come home and find his wife and/or children brutally slain. I think that the killer struck very quickly. As indicated by Mrs. Otero&#39;s fingernails, she fought with all her soul to  release herself to protect her children. What is amazing is that BTK could so adeptly overpower individuals trained in the martial arts. His type of training is not given in Boy Scouts. <BR> <BR>He appears to have taken more time with Josephine and she probably died last. I think that he is Anglo, as the postal clerk would have noted otherwise. But we all wait. I don&#39;t think that he is going to make a mistake and get caught. It will be a fluke if he is id&#39;d. And flukes do happen. Identifying him would have been more likely many years ago when memories were sharper and more people still alive who knew him. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1646-->
<!--Post: 1648--><!--Time: 1102522319-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1648"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ace<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ace<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 08, 2004 - 8:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Teardrop I respect your opinion but to me this is nothing but a sex crime and obviously Josephine was the intended target. She was sexual assaulted found only with her socks and shirt on hanging from a pipe. I can assure you he experimented with her in a sexual manner. In order to get to Josephine he had to do them all in. The BTK controled his victims with a weapon &#40;pistol&#41;probably a 22 cal single action. That&#39;s why the Otero&#39;s didn&#39;t fight. I base my opinion on facts, the fact none of the other victims in the house were sexually assaulted. No No No Josephine is what he was after and he killed the others to get to his intended target. I agree Teardrop the Otero family probably knew the killer and that was also a reason in killing them all.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1648-->
<!--Post: 2946--><!--Time: 1104304329-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2946"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dorothy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dorothy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 28, 2004 - 11:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->to Ace.... <BR>it was revealed in BTK&#39;s letter giving more details on the Otero murders that the daughter was not his target.  This info can be found in the KAKE reports. Police stated they were apparently wrong about that theory. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2946-->
<!--Post: 3150--><!--Time: 1104517368-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3150"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Thinker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Thinker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 10:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There have been rumors in Wichita from persons with police contacts that the entire carpet from the Otero living room was pulled up and is, even today, rolled up and in the  evidence storage facility used by WPD.  This makes me believe that there was more than one bloody footprint.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3150-->
<!--Post: 3230--><!--Time: 1104643427-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3230"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oliver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oliver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 01, 2005 - 9:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If Josephine was the intended target, how could BTK have possibly known that she was sick the day of the murders?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3230-->
<!--Post: 3232--><!--Time: 1104645115-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3232"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 01, 2005 - 9:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good question, Oliver. <BR> <BR>I wonder what time Josephine was scheduled to go into work?  Anyone know? <BR> <BR>If, for instance, she wasn&#39;t scheduled to go in until 10:00 AM, then perhaps BTK was just attacking her before work.  The police estimated the time of the murders was between 8:00 and 9:00 AM.  Or maybe that was the time they estimated that BTK arrived?  Either way, depending on what time she was due to go to work, he might not have had any idea she&#39;d called in sick.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3232-->
<!--Post: 3282--><!--Time: 1104733528-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3282"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 02, 2005 - 10:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->JuJuree, Josephine was the 11 year old daughter of Joseph &amp; Julie Otero. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3282-->
<!--Post: 3286--><!--Time: 1104736016-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3286"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 02, 2005 - 11:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You&#39;re right, Q.  TYVM.  Too many &#34;J&#39;s&#34; involved here!  Of course, I meant &#34;Julie.&#34;  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3286-->
<!--Post: 3893--><!--Time: 1105403792-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3893"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 10, 2005 - 4:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;Then, he sits in the house all night with a psychic and another detective hoping the killer returns to the scene. The way he loves to play games, that would be the ultimate.&#34;  <BR> <BR>I just CAN NOT understang HOW a psychic got into that Oteros house in a cupple of houers, and WITH the police???!!! <BR>I mean since WHEN have the police worked with psychics from DAY ONE??? No way! <BR> <BR>Maybe it was one of Julie Oteros friends? Julie Otero practiced hypnosis,so maybe it was her friend? <BR> <BR>Still VERY weired! <BR> <BR>skov <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3893-->
<!--Post: 6499--><!--Time: 1107833179-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6499"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 7:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->FYI Charie Otero lived in the basement,that is where his room was, and the basment was all remodeled , at least that is what I understod from an interviw with Charie Otero. <BR> <BR>Another thing maybe BTK was in som kind of possision that he could prepare som of the victims food or drinking &#40;maybe worked at a fastfood store , restorant ect, I am here think of that both som of the Oteros and Vians was sick the day of their muder. Did he put somthing in their food or drinking to make them week for the next day that he had pland to kill them?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6499-->
<!--Post: 6535--><!--Time: 1107870257-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6535"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lazysean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lazysean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 5:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->None of the Oteros were sick, Joseph II and Josephine went to a different school than the other children and just hadn&#39;t left yet.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6535-->
<!--Post: 6542--><!--Time: 1107877921-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6542"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 7:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well I don´t know what is correct about this on the net, it says that the two siblings Joseph II and Josephine was ill that day: <BR> <BR><a href="http://64.233.183.104/search?q=cache:ZqpMAXt8y_sJ:afterhourswithjasonworkman.com/archives/000127.html%2B%22been%2Bfeeling%2Bill%2Band%2Bhad%2Bstayed%2Bhome%2B%22&amp;hl=en" target=_top>http://64.233.183.104/search?q=cache:ZqpMAXt8y_sJ: afterhourswithjasonworkman.com/archives/000127.htm l&#43;%22been&#43;feeling&#43;ill&#43;and&#43;had&#43;stayed&#43;home&#43;%22&amp;hl=e n</a> <BR>Taken from the Crime Library: <BR> <BR>On January 15, 1974, a chilly yet peaceful winter day, 15-year-old Charlie Otero began his walk home from school. Charlie, his parents, Joseph and Julie and his younger siblings lived in a quiet peaceful suburban neighborhood in a small frame house located at 803 North Edgemoor Street. <BR> <BR>Charlie, happy that another school day had come to an end, walked gingerly up the side walk towards his home. His two younger siblings had been feeling ill and had stayed home from school that day <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6542-->
<!--Post: 6572--><!--Time: 1107897944-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6572"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lazysean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lazysean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 1:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well, I guess it&#39;s still possible, but in several of Charlie Otero&#39;s recent interviews he has mentioned that if they were sick he did not know it.  The older children had gone to school even earlier than usual; Joseph II and Josephine had not been out of bed yet when he left.  Here&#39;s a transcript: <a href="http://psychesknot.typepad.com/psyches_knot/2005/02/btk_the_cereal_.html" target=_top>http://psychesknot.typepad.com/psyches_knot/2005/0 2/btk_the_cereal_.html</a> -- scroll down to read the interview. <BR> <BR>There are also usually references to lunches packed up and sitting on the counter, which to me also indicates the younger children were still planning to go to school as usual. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6572-->
<!--Post: 6672--><!--Time: 1107951366-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6672"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 4:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;The older children had gone to school even earlier than usual&#34; <BR> <BR>Does anyone know why?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6672-->
<!--Post: 6687--><!--Time: 1107962146-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6687"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lazysean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lazysean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 7:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think Charlie said there was some mid-term type testing going on, and they wanted to go in early and prep for it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6687-->
<!--Post: 7075--><!--Time: 1108172241-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7075"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Purple<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Purple<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 5:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I took a class from Landwehr at wsu.  He stated from the beginning that WPD does not use psychics.  So the fact that they openly state that there was one in the house the night after the murders is odd.  Perhaps he is talking about the policy now.   <BR>I found the fact that someone thought it a shoddy neighborhood odd.  Looking back to when the crimes occurred that was a good neighborhood.  The houses were all well maintained and some of the houses just to the north on edgemoor are quite nice.  The neighborhood has indeed gone downhill since then but when the Otero&#39;s moved into that neighborhood it was a nice place to live in Wichita.   <BR>As for the light switch being downstairs.  I find that really strange.  I have lived in Wichita most of my life and I have never been in a house that did not have switch for the basement at the top of the stairs.  Even in the shoddy areas of town.  It may have been that BTK disabled the switch or unscrewed the light bulb, and they were having to look for an alternate light switch.   <BR>Finally,  I am certain, that in order to enter the house and do more than a cursory search, even though they are aware that there is a murder or murders.  The police department has to wait for a search warrant.  Given that Charlie came home from school about &#40;1.5 miles&#41; walking, he probably made it to the house about 4:15 to 4:30.  The police could not go into the house until the warrant was issued.   This would have made it after dark before they got in there to investigate.  Look at those poor kids that the Carr brothers shot in the field away from their house, the police couldn&#39;t go into that house until a search warrant was issued.   <BR> <BR>Just a few thought to clear up some things.   Not meaning to offend anyone.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7075-->
<!--Post: 7107--><!--Time: 1108184783-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7107"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 9:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->They would enter imediately because 1&#41;one or more of the victims might still be alive. 2&#41;The murderer might still be in the house. If they could see from, the open door, that there was evidence of a crime &#40;or in this case were informed by a resident&#41; they could enter. If for any reason I am wrong on the preceeding assumptions, Joe Cop can go to any house with probable cause of a crime being committed and &#39;ask&#39; to search the house, and if the resident says &#39;yes&#39; &#40;preferably in front of a witness&#41; a warrant is not required.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7107-->
<!--Post: 8508--><!--Time: 1109180278-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8508"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 9:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If BTK is so smart then why in the world would anyone think he would come back to the scene of a crime that night. There is something strange about this, unless there were murders before this. I took criminal justice for two years, rule number one dont touch anything or step in the evidence<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8508-->
